  <prompt>Port H5DataverseEnvCreationHandler.cs's collaborator PacAdminDataverseEnvCreator (pac admin create-environment --name/--region/--type/--tenant/--domain --json, PacAdminDataverseEnvCreator.cs:120-132) to raw HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential against the Power Platform Admin (BAP) API: PUT/POST .../scopes/admin/environments + async operation polling. CRITICAL PRECEDENT: this project's OWN scripts/Provision-Customer.ps1 STEP 5 (line 589) is LITERALLY TITLED 'Creating Dataverse environment via Power Platform Admin API' -- the script itself has ALREADY abandoned pac for this REST sequence; PORT THAT EXACT SEQUENCE, do not design a new one. PRESERVE the existing (already real) health probe collaborator unchanged.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Power Platform BAP admin REST API for environment creation + async LRO polling, ported from an in-repo PowerShell precedent that already made the same SDK-vs-CLI decision.</role>

  <goal>H5DataverseEnvCreationHandler.cs's environment-creation collaborator is a pure HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential implementation, following Provision-Customer.ps1's STEP 5 REST sequence exactly (same endpoint, same async-operation polling pattern, same request-body shape). The existing (already-real) health probe is UNCHANGED. create/poll/timeout/duplicate-domain outcomes are all correctly classified.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-1b §1 (H5 row, collaborator #13) is unusually confident about this port precisely because of the in-repo precedent: 'In-house precedent already exists: Provision-Customer.ps1 STEP 5 (line 589) is literally titled Creating Dataverse environment via Power Platform Admin API -- the script itself abandoned pac for REST; port that REST sequence to HttpClient.' DS-4 §4 places H5 at the head of Wave G-4's Dataverse chain because it gates everything after it (H6-&gt;H7-&gt;H10-&gt;H11-&gt;H12x).</background>
